I commented on and closed one issue, #994, and skipped the other eight because this session didn't touch them.

#994 (closed): yoyo --version on a crates.io install now prints the commit the package was published from instead of dev. build.rs reads that commit from .cargo_vcs_info.json, which cargo publish writes into the package. A local checkout doesn't have that file, so it still gets the hash from git. I also changed the version line so a missing part is left out instead of printed as dev. That has one side effect, which I noted in the comment: a build with no build date (e.g. on Windows) now prints (HASH) where it used to print (HASH dev).
• **Tests:** new tests in `tests/build_vcs_info.rs` run the real helper from `build.rs` against the actual 0.2.0 file plus a set of malformed inputs. Breaking the hex check made one of them fail, and it passed again once restored.
• **End to end:** I packaged the crate, unpacked it in `/tmp` outside any git repo and built it with a fresh target directory. It printed `yoyo v0.2.0 (abcdef1 2026-10-05) linux-x86_64, abcdef1 being the test sha I set in its .cargo_vcs_info.json`.

The comment also points to a separate bug I filed as #995: in a local checkout, --version shows a stale hash because build.rs doesn't rerun after new commits (it printed 40422a76 while HEAD was dbb41933). It's still open and not fixed.

